{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Choose for us.</b> For me and for you — he placed him on equal footing with himself. From here the Sages said: let the honor of your student be as dear to you as your own. And the honor of your companion as the reverence for your teacher — from where? As it is said, ״וַיֹּאמֶר אַהֲרֹן אֶל מֹשֶׁה בִּי אֲדֹנִי״ — and was not Aaron greater than his brother, yet he treated his companion as his teacher. And reverence for your teacher as reverence for Heaven — from where? As it is said, ״אֲדֹנִי מֹשֶׁה כְּלָאֵם״ — כַּלֵּם from the world; they are liable to extermination, those who rebel against you — it is as if they rebelled against the Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>And go out to battle.</b> Go out from the cloud and do battle in it." "<b>Tomorrow.</b> At the time of battle, I stand." "<b>Choose for us men.</b> Mighty men and God-fearing men, whose merit will aid them. Another interpretation — choose for us men who know how to nullify sorceries, because the children of Amalek were sorcerers."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :register {:flags {3 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:52.258858539Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}